WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.023
A sliding window views a contiguous subarray as a live state that updates incrementally.

00:00:06.023 --> 00:00:11.636
Add the incoming element on the right and remove the outgoing element on the left.

00:00:11.636 --> 00:00:15.880
Incremental updates avoid recomputing the window from scratch.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:22.043
When the window size is fixed at K, initialize the state with the first K elements.

00:00:22.043 --> 00:00:28.520
Slide one position right by adding the new element and subtracting the element K steps back.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.040
Track the best aggregate after every single shift.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:40.221
For longest or shortest valid subarray problems, expand the right boundary and update your frequency map or sum.

00:00:40.221 --> 00:00:45.550
Use a while-loop to advance the left boundary whenever the invariant breaks.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:49.127
Record the optimal length when the window is valid.

00:00:49.433 --> 00:00:57.902
When every subsegment inside a valid window is also valid, fixing the right endpoint counts all matching left endpoints at once.

00:00:57.902 --> 00:01:03.195
A valid window from L to R contributes R minus L plus one subarrays ending at R.

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:05.444
Sum these counts across the sweep.
